 "# name: ra-gaussian-test\n# technique: test a claim no recipe certifies, at instances Sage evaluates exactly or by intervals\n# goal: sage_test KaluzaKlein.RealAnalysis.Integral.gaussian file \"ra-gaussian-test.sage\"\n# description: Sage's ∫_ℝ e^(-bx²) dx = √(π/b): √π at b = 1, √(2π) at b = 1/2\nSEED = 0  # the instances are listed, no sampling\nR = RealIntervalField(128)\ndef B(b):\n    return QQ(1 if bool(b) else 0)\nRI = RealIntervalField(256)\ndef O(values, lhs, rhs, rel='==', edge=False):\n    # symbolic values (π, e, logs, limits Sage computed) are compared by 256-bit intervals; rationals exactly\n    if any(hasattr(v, 'parent') and v.parent() is SR for v in (lhs, rhs)):\n        lhs, rhs = RI(lhs), RI(rhs)\n    return oracle_instance(*values, lhs=lhs, rhs=rhs, relation=rel, edge=edge)\nx = var('x')\ninstances = [O([str(b), '(by norm_num)'], integrate(exp(-b * x ** 2), x, -oo, oo), sqrt(pi / b), edge=(b == 1)) for b in [1, QQ(1) / 2, 2, 5]]\n",
 "sage_version": "SageMath version 10.9, Release Date: 2026-05-04",
